WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.437
The payments table is a folder of Parquet files on S3.

2
00:00:06.437 --> 00:00:09.412
Every night, the batch job adds a few more.

3
00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:11.561
A query wants one day's total.

4
00:00:11.561 --> 00:00:18.564
With every day mixed in one folder, the engine can't tell which files hold that day, so it opens all of them.

5
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:25.199
Three years in, that's 1,095 days of files read, to answer a question about one.

6
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.826
So split the folder.

7
00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:33.243
Each day gets its own subfolder, named after the column and its value: dt equals the date.

8
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:40.265
Now the query for the seventh of November reads one folder and skips every other one, without opening a file.

9
00:00:40.265 --> 00:00:41.840
That's partition pruning.

10
00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:45.909
To skip folders, the engine first needs their list.

11
00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:56.319
S3 lists at most 1,000 names per request, so a table split by day and hour into 30,000 folders costs 30 requests before any data is read.

12
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:05.936
Hive keeps that list in the metastore: a database that maps each table name to its columns, its location, and one row per partition.

13
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:13.294
The engine sends its filter along, and the metastore answers from its own table: one partition, with its folder.

14
00:01:13.294 --> 00:01:15.799
Then the engine lists only that folder.

15
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.123
Now the metastore holds the truth.

16
00:01:18.123 --> 00:01:22.806
A late job writes the eighth of November straight to S3 and never tells it.

17
00:01:22.806 --> 00:01:27.177
A query for that day gets zero rows, though the files are right there.

18
00:01:27.333 --> 00:01:30.389
ALTER TABLE ADD PARTITION registers it.

19
00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:35.795
MSCK REPAIR TABLE finds it by listing the whole location: slow again.

20
00:01:35.967 --> 00:01:38.924
And the metastore knows folders, not files.

21
00:01:38.924 --> 00:01:46.903
The engine still lists each folder it reads, so a day of 50,000 small files costs 50 requests before the first byte.

22
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.849
Partitions let a filter skip whole folders.

23
00:01:49.849 --> 00:01:55.284
Listing them is what stays slow, which is why the folder list lives in the metastore.
